Chapter: Bench RegRight
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Codex chapter General

Section: Definitions

 Body is (regright(n-1)) * n - n: the recursive call result is a dead
 temp on the left of both the multiply and the subtract, with n a
 register-local on the right. Both are reg-right in-place folds (imul
 rax,rbx then sub rax,rbx with no staging mov). Subtraction is the
 case unique to the reg-right path -- non-commutative, the dead temp
 is the minuend and lands in the destination.

  regright : Integer -> Integer
  regright (n) = if n <= 0 then 1 else (regright (n - 1)) * n - n

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (show (regright 12))
  end

